If I would be in Poland, 1800s, I would not try to do it the Sepharadi way,

01:18:51.840 --> 01:18:53.040
because it would collapse.

01:18:53.940 --> 01:18:56.760
The going would chop my head, all right?

01:18:56.760 --> 01:19:04.760
Now, but today we are in America, and America wants everybody to be pluralistic.

01:19:04.760 --> 01:19:11.760
Hence, the Jew has a golden opportunity. Nothing to do with, you don't have to be Sepharadi or not Sepharadi.

01:19:11.760 --> 01:19:13.760
That's my view on this matter.

01:19:13.760 --> 01:19:20.760
The problem is, the question becomes, I mean, that's a certain analysis, which is too quick, because, you know,

01:19:20.760 --> 01:19:29.760
It's just man for all seasons. You know, you're saying, and it's very well taken, and in different scenarios, you act differently.

01:19:29.760 --> 01:19:30.760
That's right.

01:19:30.760 --> 01:19:31.760
If I understand it correctly.

01:19:31.760 --> 01:19:32.760
That's correct.

01:19:32.760 --> 01:19:39.760
But what happens is, as I understand history, is that there is an intellectual miscalculation.

01:19:39.760 --> 01:19:47.760
And it has ended always in the persecution of society, and the Jew being kicked out.

01:19:47.760 --> 01:19:49.700
And there is an inherent danger of that.

01:19:50.240 --> 01:19:55.560
Yes, like you're saying, as we see it and we're inspired by it,

01:19:56.500 --> 01:20:01.560
but it seems that the end result of it, at some point, is the persecuting society.

01:20:03.320 --> 01:20:06.760
And what is the response?

01:20:07.520 --> 01:20:12.520
First of all, I agree that in our case, we were persecuted,

01:20:12.980 --> 01:20:15.640
but unfortunately, we were persecuted by other Jews.

01:20:15.640 --> 01:20:21.160
and I think that when we talk about anti-semitism there is Christian of

01:20:21.160 --> 01:20:24.700
course under some it is a Muslim but it's also Jewish and anti-semitism and

01:20:24.700 --> 01:20:31.000
the Jews have to become learn to be tolerant of other Jews and not because I

01:20:31.000 --> 01:20:36.100
don't like double-breasted suit I should basically say everybody was was a

01:20:36.100 --> 01:20:43.180
Italian cut suit is an apicals then permeating all over them permeating the

01:20:43.180 --> 01:20:49.660
society but we created that strategy on alternative is something which I thank

01:20:49.660 --> 01:20:53.620
God that is a fake out there is a desire but when you see the Jews coming from

01:20:53.620 --> 01:21:01.040
Russia today and non-polaristic strategy was you know they are bereft of every

01:21:01.040 --> 01:21:07.780
single value they don't have one single Jewish family thank God that Israel not

01:21:07.780 --> 01:21:15.160
only will absorb and these people will become full Jews or they are already some of them

01:21:15.160 --> 01:21:29.920
already full Jews and I am a professor at Valley United and I see some of these Russian students are brilliant and God bless them and this but when they keep doing them we're going to lose some in this game

01:21:29.920 --> 01:21:39.920
We're going to do the same. But that's part of life. We cannot ensure that every single Jew is going to survive every single hurdle.

01:21:39.920 --> 01:21:49.920
But if we don't do that, we're going to become disenchanted with Judaism. We're going to start thinking of Judaism in mythical terms,

01:21:49.920 --> 01:22:00.120
in magical terms, in black magic, a religion of unenlightened minds.

01:22:00.920 --> 01:22:06.200
And only people who are not too clever will accept Judaism.

01:22:06.760 --> 01:22:10.520
How do you expect somebody who goes to a university in the States

01:22:10.520 --> 01:22:15.660
and reads the great masterpieces of American literature, English literature, philosophy, science,

01:22:15.660 --> 01:22:22.660
and then goes to a Talmud Tora where they, what they have to teach them about Judaism is almost borders into witchcraft.

01:22:22.660 --> 01:22:27.660
So how this person is going to, to, to, to this child,

01:22:27.660 --> 01:22:32.660
the natural tendency would be to veer towards American culture.

01:22:32.660 --> 01:22:35.660
He would say, yes, Judaism is something, you know,

01:22:35.660 --> 01:22:41.660
Bar Minan, when somebody plays a way, go to a Jewish Ribbi to bury the person. That's about it.

01:22:41.660 --> 01:22:50.660
But if you cannot speak to this boy or girl in a way that makes sense to him according to his American values,

01:22:50.660 --> 01:22:57.660
to the standards of American universities, you're going to lose this person. That's what I feel.

01:22:57.660 --> 01:23:07.660
And in this sense, living in America is a challenge. Otherwise, just like the Christian lost their elite to Islam,

01:23:07.660 --> 01:23:10.660
We are losing our elite to American culture.

01:23:10.660 --> 01:23:13.660
We become assimilated. It's the same thing.

01:23:13.660 --> 01:23:18.660
I mean, we have Cardoso, Benjamin Cardoso,

01:23:18.660 --> 01:23:24.660
was the president of the Sepharadi community and was a member of the Supreme Court.

01:23:24.660 --> 01:23:31.660
And when he writes his justice, his legal decision, he writes like a ha-ham.

01:23:31.660 --> 01:23:38.660
The whole notion of equity, of ethics in American law was introduced by Benjamin Cardoso.

01:23:41.460 --> 01:23:48.460
And I read his writings because I was a professor of Jewish law for 20 years and you can see

01:23:48.460 --> 01:23:55.460
he paraphrases Mishna, he paraphrases Gemara. He does it very proudly. Indian people, Benjamin

01:23:55.460 --> 01:24:05.940
Indian people, Benjamin Cardoso, we wear our paragatas, the special kind of sneakers, slippers,

01:24:06.420 --> 01:24:13.200
because he was the president of the community, and as a good Jew, he was proud of his heritage.

01:24:14.540 --> 01:24:20.600
Now, he did not betray American ideals, and he did not betray Jewish ideals.

01:24:21.500 --> 01:24:24.060
So he did it. Why can't we do it?

01:24:24.060 --> 01:24:27.060
that's

01:24:32.760 --> 01:24:36.320
very much involved

01:24:37.220 --> 01:24:45.920
I think or let me ask you to breathe that the reason that they have a

01:24:45.920 --> 01:24:51.180
tendency to go in this direction which I think they do some wonderful things but

01:24:51.180 --> 01:24:57.180
open-mindedness was not one of their virtues, is the fact that we have not given them anything

01:24:57.180 --> 01:25:02.180
that our most part of youth, anything new to hang their hat on.

01:25:02.180 --> 01:25:14.180
I agree fully, 100% with you. It's inexcusable that we have not provided for our children.

01:25:14.180 --> 01:25:29.620
We did not give them an opportunity to become part of a living tradition. And because we did not take care of them, we left them in the street. We gave birth to them and Jewishly we put them in the street.

01:25:29.620 --> 01:25:34.620
And then the Hasidim, they have something to offer them.

01:25:34.620 --> 01:25:40.620
And these people are looking, searching for identity, for values.

01:25:40.620 --> 01:25:45.620
We, instead of, I don't like to, I don't criticize, never only the Hasidim, you know,

01:25:45.620 --> 01:25:49.620
because at least they're doing something, they're doing what they know how to do.

01:25:49.620 --> 01:25:58.620
The question is why we did not offer some intelligent objectivity.

01:25:58.620 --> 01:26:05.620
This is exactly it. I know that in Bronx, New York, we had a big Sepharadi Brotherhood,

01:26:05.620 --> 01:26:12.620
2,500 members. We were the most organized people, unburied, not dead, anywhere in the world.

01:26:12.620 --> 01:26:17.620
Nobody ever was unburied for more than 24 hours unless there was some extinguishing

01:26:17.620 --> 01:26:24.620
yeshivas. But we didn't have one East Camp, we didn't have one yeshiva, we didn't give

01:26:24.620 --> 01:26:30.820
give one kid a scholarship to go to any yeshiva, Sepharadi or otherwise. We didn't form one

01:26:30.820 --> 01:26:36.420
Sepharadi yeshiva. In all the years, the only example we've ever had in this country was

01:26:36.420 --> 01:26:42.000
go to Ashkenaz camps, and thank God we had them. To go to Ashkenaz yeshivot, and I guess

01:26:42.000 --> 01:26:46.820
thank God we had them too. I said to my kids, if I didn't have that, we would have had nothing.

01:26:47.400 --> 01:26:53.700
But we have done almost nothing for ourselves. We have been takers and not givers or doers

01:26:53.700 --> 01:26:56.040
for the last 75 years in this country.

01:26:56.940 --> 01:26:59.840
And the reason I'm saying this, I'm on a soapbox,

01:26:59.980 --> 01:27:05.620
is maybe tonight, because Ribbi Fawor, 45 years ago,

01:27:07.060 --> 01:27:09.660
came to our Sepharadi synagogue in the Bronx

01:27:09.660 --> 01:27:14.360
and tried to unify the Brooklyn Syrian Jews,

01:27:14.860 --> 01:27:16.960
the Sepharadi community in the Bronx,

01:27:17.440 --> 01:27:19.900
and we had a very small start, but it petered out.

01:27:19.900 --> 01:27:25.280
In Miami, there are four or five, in the Miami area between Fort Lauderdale and Fort

01:27:25.280 --> 01:27:31.900
V, Sepharadi City. We have not had one meeting, we have not done one thing to

01:27:31.900 --> 01:27:38.820
unify our youth. If we don't do it in this generation, ain't no next generation. So

01:27:38.820 --> 01:27:45.140
perhaps because Ribbi Thor is here, maybe our boards can get together, maybe we

01:27:45.140 --> 01:27:49.520
could revive ourselves from the dead and go forward with the heritage we have in

01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:51.420
the modern way, he says.

01:27:51.880 --> 01:27:53.560
Or, we could say this

01:27:53.560 --> 01:27:54.860
was a wonderful meeting tonight.

01:27:55.720 --> 01:27:57.060
I'd like the Ribbi to speak.

01:27:57.240 --> 01:27:59.440
He's given all the lectures all over town.

01:28:00.060 --> 01:28:01.400
And we'll see him in 10 years

01:28:01.400 --> 01:28:02.740
if there's anybody left to see him.

01:28:04.860 --> 01:28:07.480
I agree

01:28:07.480 --> 01:28:09.520
with you. And just let me add

01:28:09.520 --> 01:28:10.900
something. You know,

01:28:12.940 --> 01:28:15.200
again,

01:28:17.160 --> 01:28:19.380
one of the beautiful things among

01:28:19.380 --> 01:28:35.380
the Sepharadi is that we love music. We love music. We love food. We love to have a good time.

01:28:35.380 --> 01:28:46.380
But we don't say a specific type of music. We should learn how to love different styles of Sepharadi music, different styles of food.

01:28:46.380 --> 01:28:51.380
food. Not always the body, but also what's going on. And let's have the children get together,

01:28:51.380 --> 01:29:00.380
know each other, and in other words, let me be blunt, we are the giants.

01:29:00.380 --> 01:29:04.380
They are the dwarves.

01:29:04.380 --> 01:29:08.380
It's difficult, I just take it down so many times. We climb on our shoulders.

01:29:08.380 --> 01:29:12.380
But they're plowing our shoulders.

01:29:12.380 --> 01:29:19.380
One of the things I like, I insisted, and I was successful in Brooklyn, now it becomes a kind of place.

01:29:19.380 --> 01:29:21.380
But Minyan for the children.

01:29:21.380 --> 01:29:24.380
We don't have to serve in Iraq.

01:29:24.380 --> 01:29:27.380
But we don't have to have our own choir.

01:29:27.380 --> 01:29:33.380
We have to have the ground for the people, the boys and girls to know what we feel.

01:29:33.380 --> 01:29:37.380
To share the different traditions, the different things.

01:29:37.380 --> 01:29:41.380
They're going to be more intelligent than we are, that's for sure.

01:29:41.380 --> 01:29:48.380
So, let me show you some Jewish orientation.

01:29:48.380 --> 01:29:53.380
Being Sefer Adi is a responsibility.

01:29:53.380 --> 01:30:01.380
Because it means you want to be Jewish 100%, and American or whatever it is, 100%.

01:30:01.380 --> 01:30:04.380
I feel myself 100% American.

01:30:04.380 --> 01:30:18.380
I love America, not 99%, 100%. I'm being proud of America. But I think, to be honest, that I love America so much because I am Jewish.

01:30:18.380 --> 01:30:25.380
Because my Judaism teaches me to appreciate what this country has done for all of us.

01:30:25.380 --> 01:30:31.380
So I don't see any contradiction between being American and being Jewish.

01:30:31.380 --> 01:30:36.680
On the contrary, I think that also I'm a better Jew because I'm an American.

01:30:36.680 --> 01:30:40.680
I learned a lot about Judaism just by living in America.

01:30:40.680 --> 01:30:43.480
So I don't see this contradiction.

01:30:43.480 --> 01:30:51.080
I think that this is something, another chance for a golden age.

01:30:51.080 --> 01:30:53.580
Really a golden age.

01:30:53.580 --> 01:30:57.980
And this is again, the ball is in our court.

01:30:57.980 --> 01:31:01.180
Nobody wants to play it. They cannot accept us.

01:31:01.180 --> 01:31:02.180
My problem.

01:31:02.180 --> 01:31:03.180
Yes.

01:31:03.180 --> 01:31:05.180
Is it possible to make your proposition?

01:31:08.180 --> 01:31:10.180
I would like to answer directly the question.

01:31:10.180 --> 01:31:12.180
No, no, I'm glad that he is a man.

01:31:12.180 --> 01:31:13.180
All right?

01:31:13.180 --> 01:31:14.180
No.

01:31:14.180 --> 01:31:15.180
No.

01:31:15.180 --> 01:31:23.180
I would like to answer, you know, to the gentleman about his worries, because we are several

01:31:23.180 --> 01:31:30.180
Sepharadi communities, but I don't see, you know, an entity of coordination between them.

01:31:30.180 --> 01:31:34.940
My proposition is this. We would like to hire you as a coordinator.
